<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>AI agent · Agentic Bible</title><meta name="description" content="A system that uses a model to choose actions, observe their results, and work toward a goal within defined limits."><meta property="og:title" content="AI agent · Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:description" content="A system that uses a model to choose actions, observe their results, and work toward a goal within defined limits."><meta property="og:type" content="article"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:url" content="https://agenticbible.si/articles/ai-agent/"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary"><meta name="twitter:title" content="AI agent · Agentic Bible"><meta name="twitter:description" content="A system that uses a model to choose actions, observe their results, and work toward a goal within defined limits."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><link rel="canonical" href="https://agenticbible.si/articles/ai-agent/"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TechArticle","headline":"AI agent","description":"A system that uses a model to choose actions, observe their results, and work toward a goal within defined limits.","articleSection":"Foundations","inLanguage":"en","url":"https://agenticbible.si/articles/ai-agent/","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://agenticbible.si/articles/ai-agent/"},"citation":["https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents","https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.03629","https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/overview"]}</script><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/Base.DyzAbnuc.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/_id_.w1YKO1jA.css"></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header shell"><a class="wordmark" href="/"><img src="/favicon.svg" width="36" height="36" alt=""><span>Agentic Bible<span class="wordmark-sub">A living reference</span></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/" aria-current="page">Library</a><a href="/topics/">Topics</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/history/">History</a></nav><a class="header-search" href="/search/" aria-label="Search the library"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></circle><path d="m13 13 4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></path></svg><span>Search</span><kbd aria-hidden="true">/</kbd></a></header><div class="preview-strip" role="region" aria-label="Edition status"><div class="shell"><span class="status-dot"></span> Preview edition <span class="strip-detail">Sourced working drafts. Editorial review pending.</span></div></div><main id="main" class="shell" tabindex="-1"><div class="article-breadcrumb" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Library</a><span data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>/</span><a href="/topics/foundations/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Foundations</a></div><div class="reading-layout" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><article class="article" data-pagefind-body data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><header id="overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-pagefind-meta="topic" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Foundations / Reference entry 01</p><h1 data-pagefind-meta="title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>AI agent</h1><p class="article-deck" data-pagefind-meta="description" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>A system that uses a model to choose actions, observe their results, and work toward a goal within defined limits.</p><div class="article-status" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="draft-pill" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="status-dot" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></span> Working draft</span><span data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Human editorial certification pending</span></div><nav class="article-actions" aria-label="Article actions" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="#sources" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources (3)</a><a href="#revision" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision history</a><a href="#share" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Share or cite</a><a href="/contribute/?article=ai-agent" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Contribution options</a></nav></header><aside class="contents" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><details data-article-contents data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><summary data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>On this page</summary><nav aria-label="On this page" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="#overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Overview</a><a href="#the-actionobservation-loop" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The action–observation loop</a><a href="#agent-or-workflow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Agent or workflow?</a><a href="#tools-and-authority" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Tools and authority</a><a href="#how-to-evaluate-a-claim" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>How to evaluate a claim</a><a href="#sources" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources & context</a><a href="#revision" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision record</a></nav></details><div class="contents-bottom" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Part of the collection</span><a href="/topics/foundations/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Foundations <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></a></div></aside><div class="prose" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p>An <strong>AI agent</strong> is a system that uses a model to select actions, receives feedback from its environment, and continues toward a goal. In this encyclopedia, the term describes a pattern of control. It does not imply consciousness, unlimited independence, or reliable judgment. Definitions vary: Anthropic distinguishes model-directed agents from workflows whose paths are fixed in code. <a href="#source-patterns">1</a></p>
<h2 id="the-actionobservation-loop">The action–observation loop</h2>
<p>A task starts with an objective and a set of available actions. The model may request an action, the surrounding software executes it, and the result becomes input for the next decision. A stop condition ends the loop. Anthropic describes environmental feedback and bounded iteration as practical ingredients of this pattern. <a href="#source-patterns">1</a></p>
<p>The ReAct research paper explored interleaving reasoning and actions so a language model could interact with external environments. Its experiments are evidence for particular methods on particular benchmarks, rather than proof that every agent is dependable. <a href="#source-react">2</a></p>
<p>Consider an illustrative library assistant asked to investigate a broken citation. It could open the cited page, inspect a replacement source, and propose an edit with evidence. A successful run would leave a reviewable correction and an explanation of its sources. A failed fetch should remain a failed fetch; generating a plausible replacement URL would not complete the task.</p>
<h2 id="agent-or-workflow">Agent or workflow?</h2>
<p>The useful question is who chooses the next step. A workflow might always retrieve a document, summarize it, and pass the summary to a reviewer. An agent can choose another retrieval after inspecting the first result. Real systems can combine these approaches. Anthropic’s taxonomy is a helpful architectural distinction, not a universally agreed definition. <a href="#source-patterns">1</a></p>
<p>More autonomy also creates more possible failure paths. A fixed workflow can be easier to test when a task has predictable steps. Anthropic recommends adding complexity only when the task benefits justify the extra latency and cost. <a href="#source-patterns">1</a></p>
<h2 id="tools-and-authority">Tools and authority</h2>
<p><a href="/articles/tool-use/">Tool use</a> supplies the actions in many agent loops. With client-side tools, the model returns a structured request and the application executes it. That boundary gives the application a place to validate arguments, enforce permissions, and reject an operation. A tool request is not itself proof that an operation happened. <a href="#source-tools">3</a></p>
<p><a href="/articles/model-context-protocol/">Model Context Protocol</a> is one way to connect such capabilities. An agent can also use ordinary application functions. The protocol choice and the decision to allow an action are separate design questions.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-evaluate-a-claim">How to evaluate a claim</h2>
<p>For this project, we propose evaluating agents against an observable outcome: did a correction have valid evidence, did it preserve history, and did the system stop within its limits? These are editorial design criteria, not measurements from a deployed pipeline.</p>
<p>An evaluation should make the task, environment, allowed actions, failure cases, and budget explicit. A fluent final answer alone would not show whether a citation was checked. The long-term Agentic Bible goal includes bounded autonomous maintenance; this first slice implements reading and search only.</p>
</div><p class="article-feedback" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="/contribute/?article=ai-agent" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Suggest a correction or primary source</a> · Public intake remains on hold; the local synthetic form covers only the original three entries.</p><section class="sources" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Follow the evidence</p><h2 id="sources-title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources & context</h2><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Primary sources checked on <time datetime="2026-10-16" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>16 October 2026</time>. A source check is not independent editorial approval.</p><ol data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><li id="source-patterns" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Building effective agents <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Anthropic</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Published 19 December 2024; architectural patterns, not a current SDK reference.</p></li><li id="source-react" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.03629" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>ReAct: Synergizing Reasoning and Acting in Language Models <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Yao et al., arXiv</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Research first submitted October 2022; results apply to the paper’s evaluated tasks.</p></li><li id="source-tools" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Tool use with Claude <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Anthropic</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Living API documentation; consulted for the client-tool execution boundary.</p></li></ol></section><section class="revision" id="revision" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><h2 data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision record</h2><dl data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Authorship</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>AI-assisted project draft</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Source check</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><time datetime="2026-10-16" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>16 October 2026</time>. This records source consultation, not editorial certification.</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Human editorial review</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Pending. No human editorial certification is recorded.</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Latest source change</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><time datetime="2026-10-17" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>17 October 2026</time> · Add six sourced entries on agent operating principles · <code data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>54b9d079</code></dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision receipt</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>No separate publication receipt is recorded for this working draft.</dd></div></dl><p class="review-scope" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The twenty entries received deep reading across external and internal review. Claim verification was sampled; this does not certify every factual claim.</p><a class="text-link" data-source-commit="8a38252384c6fe6024a75b462ad95294a131100c" href="https://github.com/Leshey-Digital/agentic-bible/commits/8a38252384c6fe6024a75b462ad95294a131100c/src/content/articles/ai-agent.md" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>View file history on GitHub <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></a></section><section class="share-tools" id="share" aria-labelledby="share-title" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Keep a useful reference</p><h2 id="share-title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Share or cite this entry</h2><p id="article-citation" tabindex="0" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>“AI agent.” Agentic Bible. https://agenticbible.si/articles/ai-agent/</p><div class="share-buttons" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><button type="button" data-copy-link hidden data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Copy article link</button><button type="button" data-copy-citation hidden data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Copy citation</button></div><p class="share-status" data-share-status role="status" aria-live="polite" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The citation and link above remain available to copy manually if clipboard access is unavailable.</p></section><section class="related" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Keep exploring</p><h2 data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Connected ideas</h2><a href="/articles/tool-use/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxf